Below is a **step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, tooling recommendations, and best‑practice patterns.  

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Design

| What | Why | How |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Define core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, cart, checkout, user profile, reviews, admin panel | Write a feature list; prioritize MVP items |
| **Create user personas & flows** | Understand how different users will interact | Sketch flows in Figma/Adobe XD |
| **Wireframe & prototype** | Validate layout before coding | Use Figma + FigJam; share with stakeholders |
| **Design system / style guide** | Consistent UI, faster dev | Build a component library (Storybook) or use a UI kit (Chakra UI, Material‑UI) |

> **Tip:** Keep the design modular. Atomic design (atoms → molecules → organisms) works great for reusable components.

---

## 2️⃣ Tech Stack Decision

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular | **React** (most community, ecosystem) |
| **SSR / SSG** | Next.js, Remix, Nuxt | **Next.js** (React + SSR + SSG + API routes) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, React Query | **Redux Toolkit** for global state + **React Query** for server data |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS, CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Emotion | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast) |
| **Type system** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (type safety, IDE support) |
| **Bundler** | Vite, Webpack, Next.js built‑in | **Next.js** (bundles automatically) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress, Playwright | Unit: **Jest + RTL**; E2E: **Cypress** |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | **GitHub Actions** (free for public repos) |
| **Deployment** | Vercel, Netlify, Render, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (native Next.js support) |
| **CMS / Headless** | Contentful, Strapi, Sanity, Prismic | **Strapi** (self‑hosted, flexible) |
| **Payments** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (API, Checkout, Elements) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Hotjar | **Google Analytics** + **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly) |
| **Accessibility** | axe-core, Lighthouse | Run **axe** in CI, audit with **Lighthouse** |

---

## 3️⃣ Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend --typescript
cd ecommerce-frontend
```

### Folder structure

```
/components   # UI components (atoms, molecules)
  /ui         # generic UI primitives
  /layout     # page layouts
  /product    # product card, detail
  /cart       # cart sidebar, item list
/pages        # Next.js pages
  /api        # serverless API routes (e.g., auth, checkout)
  /products   # product listing, detail
  /cart       # cart page
  /checkout   # checkout flow
  /admin      # admin dashboard
  /auth       # login / signup
/public       # static assets
/styles       # global styles (Tailwind config)
/store        # Redux Toolkit slices
  /cartSlice.ts
  /productSlice.ts
  /userSlice.ts
/tests        # Jest + RTL tests
  /components
  /pages
  /store
/.github/workflows  # GitHub Actions CI/CD
```

---

## 4️⃣ Core Features Implementation

### 4.1 Product Catalog

```tsx
// components/product/ProductCard.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import Image from 'next/image';

export interface Product {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  price: number;
  imageUrl: string;
}

export const ProductCard: React.FC<{ product: Product }> = ({ product }) => (
  <Link href={`/products/${product.id}`}>
    <a className="block p-4 border rounded hover:shadow-lg transition">
      <Image src={product.imageUrl} alt={product.title} width={200} height={200} />
      <h3 className="mt-2 font-semibold">{product.title}</h3>
      <p className="text-gray-600">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
    </a>
  </Link>
);
```

**Fetching data with React Query**

```tsx
// store/productSlice.ts
import { createSlice } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import axios from 'axios';

export const fetchProducts = async () => {
  const { data } = await axios.get('/api/products');
  return data;
};

export const useProducts = () => {
  return useQuery(['products'], fetchProducts);
};
```

### 4.2 Cart & Checkout

```tsx
// store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface CartItem {
  productId: string;
  quantity: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addToCart(state, action: PayloadAction<CartItem>) {
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.productId === action.payload.productId);
      if (existing) {
        existing.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      } else {
        state.items.push(action.payload);
      }
    },
    removeFromCart(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter(i => i.productId !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addToCart, removeFromCart, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

**Checkout page with Stripe Elements**

```tsx
// pages/checkout.tsx
import { loadStripe } from '@stripe/stripe-js';
import { Elements } from '@stripe/react-stripe-js';
import CheckoutForm from '../components/checkout/CheckoutForm';

const stripePromise = loadStripe(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY!);

export default function Checkout() {
  return (
    <Elements stripe={stripePromise}>
      <CheckoutForm />
    </Elements>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// components/checkout/CheckoutForm.tsx
import { CardElement, useStripe, useElements } from '@stripe/react-stripe-js';
import { useDispatch } from 'react-redux';
import { clearCart } from '../../store/cartSlice';
import axios from 'axios';

export default function CheckoutForm() {
  const stripe = useStripe();
  const elements = useElements();
  const dispatch = useDispatch();

  const handleSubmit = async (e: React.FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (!stripe || !elements) return;

    const { error, paymentMethod } = await stripe.createPaymentMethod({
      type: 'card',
      card: elements.getElement(CardElement)!,
    });

    if (error) {
      console.error(error);
      return;
    }

    // Send paymentMethod.id to your backend
    const { data } = await axios.post('/api/checkout', { paymentMethodId: paymentMethod.id });
    if (data.success) {
      dispatch(clearCart());
      alert('Payment successful!');
    }
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className="max-w-md mx-auto">
      <CardElement className="border p-2 rounded mb-4" />
      <button type="submit" disabled={!stripe} className="bg-blue-600 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded">
        Pay
      </button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

### 4.3 Search & Filters

Use a lightweight search library (Fuse.js) or rely on backend query parameters.

```tsx
// pages/api/products.ts
import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import { prisma } from '../../lib/prisma';

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  const { q, category, minPrice, maxPrice } = req.query;
  const products = await prisma.product.findMany({
    where: {
      title: { contains: q as string, mode: 'insensitive' },
      category: { equals: category as string },
      price: {
        gte: Number(minPrice),
        lte: Number(maxPrice),
      },
    },
  });
  res.json(products);
}
```

### 4.4 Admin Dashboard

Use Next.js API routes for CRUD operations, protected by JWT or session.

```tsx
// pages/api/admin/products/[id].ts
import { getSession } from 'next-auth/react';
import { prisma } from '../../../lib/prisma';

export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const session = await getSession({ req });
  if (!session?.user?.isAdmin) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });

  const { id } = req.query;
  if (req.method === 'DELETE') {
    await prisma.product.delete({ where: { id: id as string } });
    return res.json({ success: true });
  }
  // Handle other methods...
}
```

