## 8️⃣ CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

`.github/workflows/ci.yml`

```yaml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test
      - run: npm run build
```

`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`

```yaml
name: Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: vercel/action@v1
        with:
          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
          vercel-args: '--prod'
```

---

## 9️⃣ Performance Optimizations

| Technique | How |
|-----------|-----|
| **Image Optimization** | Next.js `<Image>` component |
| **Code Splitting** | Dynamic imports (`next/dynamic`) |
| **Lazy Loading** | `loading="lazy"` on images, `IntersectionObserver` for components |
| **Prefetching** | `next/link` prefetch |
| **Service Worker** | Next.js PWA plugin or Workbox |
| **Bundle Analysis** | `next-bundle-analyzer` |
| **Tree Shaking** | ES modules, remove unused imports |

---

## 10️⃣ Deployment & Monitoring

| Service | Why |
|---------|-----|
| **Vercel** | Native Next.js support, instant preview URLs |
| **Netlify** | Alternative, easy to set up |
| **Sentry** | Error tracking |
| **LogRocket** | Session replay |
| **Datadog** | Performance monitoring |

---

## 11️⃣ Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] All core features implemented
- [ ] Responsive design tested on mobile, tablet, desktop
- [ ] Accessibility audit passed (axe, Lighthouse)
- [ ] SEO meta tags, structured data added
- [ ] Unit & integration tests coverage > 80%
- [ ] E2E tests passing
- [ ] CI pipeline builds & tests
- [ ] Deployment pipeline working
- [ ] Analytics & error monitoring integrated
- [ ] Security review (CORS, CSRF, XSS, rate limiting)
- [ ] Documentation (README, API docs, component docs)

---

## 🎉 Final Thoughts

*Start small, iterate fast.*  
Build an MVP with the essential pages (catalog, cart, checkout). Once stable, add advanced features (reviews, wishlists, admin panel).  

Keep the codebase clean: use TypeScript, linting, formatting, and a solid folder structure.  
Automate everything: CI/CD, testing, linting, accessibility checks.  

Happy coding! 🚀

---
